    "prompt": "The area of the parallelogram in the figure is 300 cm². The area of the hatched triangle is 100 cm² and that of the dotted triangle is 40 cm². What is the area, in cm², of the black triangle?",
    "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2023-g0708/q14.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "10"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "20"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "25"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "30"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "50"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Half the parallelogram",
        "body": "Call the point on the top side where the lines meet $P$. The white triangle has the whole bottom side as its base and $P$ on the opposite side, so its height is the height of the parallelogram: its area is half the parallelogram, 150 cm².\n\nThe rest, 150 cm², is made of the dotted triangle (40) and the big triangle on the left formed by the left side and $P$ (hatched + black). So hatched + black = 150 − 40 = 110, and black = 110 − 100 = 10 cm².\n\n**Answer: (A) 10**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
